ok   leftover 1046 connection removed at start, others kept
ok   no downloads: library / download / remove are unknown commands; thumb read from the cache
ok   search: TVHTML5 InnerTube, anonymous when signed out; lockups parsed; offline -> "search offline"
ok   play cached: connect + playFile + ytdec args, no fetcher
ok   clock ticks forwarded to ytdec (mono ms) and as time events
ok   pause/resume/seek/video map to SOME/IP and ytdec stdin
ok   stop disconnects audio and quits ytdec
ok   app disconnect stops within 1 s
ok   fault (uncaught error path) disconnects and goes idle
ok   ytdec dies -> one restart with seek to the clock; second death -> error, audio keeps playing
ok   no decoded frames for the watchdog period -> child restarted
ok   STOP mid-file -> held as paused; resume plays the file again at that point
ok   end of file (STOP after PLAY, near the end) -> ended, audio released
ok   play uncached: the fetcher (env {}, cwd /) into a fresh dir; preparing pct; playing after audio_ready + 10 s of video
ok   buffering: true when the clock nears the fetched video, the watchdog spares ytdec; fetcher done -> false
ok   fetcher error after playback began: one "video incomplete" error, audio plays on
ok   stop kills the fetcher
ok   speed: a warm spare takes the prefetch (stream lookup); the next spare takes the play, with --info
ok   extras: chapters + SponsorBlock (hashed prefix, cached), a segment skipped once; position kept, resumed
ok   SponsorBlock: the play's skip list; other categories (outro) only in extras, for the app's Skip button
ok   fetcher error before playable -> error state + "fetch: <msg>", nothing played
ok   fetcher error before playable: retried after a wait (retry event), then plays
ok   a refused video (unavailable) is not retried
ok   a second play during the first one's playFile keeps the second's audio
ok   head: plays audio.head.m4a on audio_head + 10 s video; audio_ready -> playFile(audio.m4a) on the same connection + setTime; head removed
ok   head: total is the video's (meta), not the head file's; switch seeks to the extrapolated clock; stale times after it ignored
ok   head: the full file's PLAY during the switch still arms its end -> ended
ok   head runs out before audio.m4a: buffering, player paused, STOP at its end is not `ended`; audio_ready resumes there
ok   preparing on the head: pct moves with the video lead
ok   seek past the head before audio.m4a: buffering, no setTime on the head; audio_ready -> playFile + setTime there
ok   paused on the head when audio.m4a arrives: no switch until resume, which plays audio.m4a at that point
ok   stop during the switch: release waits for the playFile, no setTime after, audio released
ok   a new play during the switch: the old switch does nothing more, the new video plays
ok   fetcher dies while only the head is there: error state, audio released
ok   zoom while playing: ytdec again with the other mode at the clock, no error; same mode does nothing
ok   quality while playing: fetched again at that height; same height: nothing
ok   auth_status with no account: signed out
ok   auth: creds from the base script, device code, polled until signed in; account 0600 in a dir others cannot list
ok   feed subs: TVHTML5 browse with the token; video tiles only, each once, channel and length
ok   token with < 5 min left refreshed before the browse; a 401 forces one more refresh
ok   youtube offline: feed error, still signed in
ok   refresh answered invalid_grant: signed out, account gone, the feed says so
ok   sign_out deletes the account; a code left to expire -> signed out; no creds -> auth error
ok   feed: prototype names are unknown feeds; asks while one is in flight share its browse
ok   sign_out while a refresh is in flight: the new token is not written back
ok   sign_out during the device-code request: no code, no polling
ok   sign_out while a poll is offline: not re-armed
ok   client id/secret scraped once a process; scraped again once when the device code is refused
ok   fetch uid: none without MainApp's ranges; then the lowest free above them, written for the uplink
ok   fetch uid: kept while free (its own processes do not count); taken since -> picked again; two MainApps: the running one
ok   fetch helper: spawned as the uid, the request (secrets) on stdin only, the answer from stdout
ok   fetch helper: no answer by the timeout -> killed, rejected
ok   the real helper (ytd.js --fetch): a request it cannot make comes back as an error
ok   daemon without a fetch uid: sign-in and feeds say so, nothing spawned, no crash
ok   no token, secret or device code in the log
ok   feedItems: an empty or odd answer is no items
